Question: How can a non-English speaking person book a train ticket?
Answer: Options: 1) Use IRCTC website in regional language (select from language dropdown). 2) Use RailMadad in 22+ Indian languages. 3) Visit station counter — staff speak local language. 4) Call 139 — available in Hindi and English. 5) Ask a literate friend/family member to help. 6) Future: AI voice assistant (being built).